Hi Wendy

this is by looping, but the R code is so compact that the added value of 
a specialised function might be marginal:


cn = colnames(test)
sapply(unique(cn), function(g) rowMeans(test[,cn==g,drop=FALSE]))

        A  B
[1,] 2.5 10
[2,] 3.5 11
[3,] 4.5 12


Or also:

by(t(test), colnames(test), mean)

INDICES: A
  V1  V2  V3
2.5 3.5 4.5
------------------------------------------------------------
INDICES: B
V1 V2 V3
10 11 12

Best wishes
	Wolfgang


